        "original_id": "9bfabb0a-49d3-52ef-8ed6-60fd28aa3fe2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: WWE Super Tuesday\n- Organizations: World Wrestling Entertainment (WWE)\n- Places: TD Garden, Fleet Center, Verizon Wireless Arena, Boston, Massachusetts, Manchester, New Hampshire\n- Topics: professional wrestling television specials, arena naming history\n\nFacts:\n- TD Garden opened in 1995 in Boston, Massachusetts, as a replacement for the original Boston Garden.\n- TD Garden has been known as Shawmut Center, FleetCenter, and TD Banknorth Garden, and it is often called Boston Garden and “The Garden.”\n- WWE produced Super Tuesday as a 1-hour professional wrestling television special event on 12 November 2002.\n- WWE taped Super Tuesday on November 4 and 5, 2002, at the Fleet Center in Boston, Massachusetts, and Verizon Wireless Arena in Manchester, New Hampshire.\n- WWE Super Tuesday featured matches from both Raw and SmackDown.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
